ntil-5-16 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [l] until-5-17 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-17 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<>] until-5\n","grammar_lazy":false,"grammar_triggers":[],"preserved_tokens":[248058,248059,248068,248069],"chat_format":"peg-native","reasoning_format":"deepseek","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"next_token":[{"has_next_token":false,"has_new_line":false,"n_remain":-1,"n_decoded":0}],"prompt":"<|im_start|>system\n# Aster bounded payment-recovery actor\n\nYou are the ordinary task actor for a frozen multi-region payment recovery\nworld. Use exact source observations, exact task-native work, candidate effects,\nand current checks to produce the requested decision package. Preserve units,\nprobabilities, versions, qualifications, authority, and cross-object\nrelationships.\n\nReturn exactly one declared JSON action object per response. Do not add prose,\nMarkdown fences, a second object, or hidden reasoning. Any model-authored\nsemantic register is lossy and non-authoritative. Submission is only a\nproposal; independent candidate-bound adjudication controls readiness.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Authoritative task — Aster multi-region payment recovery decision\n\nAster Payments must recover a multi-region transaction platform after ledger,\nqueue, access, and external-rail disturbances. Build and maintain the exact\ncandidate files, then propose submission only when the package is genuinely\nready for independent review.\n\nThe world contains sixteen exact, versioned source objects with opaque IDs.\nCatalog titles help navigation but do not supply findings. Read the bytes needed\nfor the work and cite sources as `[SOURCE_ID]`.\n\n## Required exact work\n\nMaintain `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md` as a compact task-native evidence and\ndecision matrix. Preserve established source-bound facts, explicit\ncross-source dependencies, conflicts, unknowns, candidate currency, and the\nexact source citations needed to review them. This work is non-authoritative.\n\nConstruct `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md` as a 1,500–2,100-word Aster\nPayment Recovery Decision with exactly the declared section headings. Use at\nleast twelve distinct source IDs and integrate—not merely list—the governing\nrelationships.\n\nAddress all twelve requirement groups:\n\n- Q01 — authority for isolation, repair, verification, traffic restoration, and closure;\n- Q02 — ledger replication, consistency, RPO/RTO, schema, writer, and settlement bindings;\n- Q03 — idempotency scopes, retry windows, duplicate controls, and queue identity;\n- Q04 — queue drain, event ordering, traffic interaction, pause/resume, and retirement;\n- Q05 — shared capacity, staged traffic ramp, dependency headroom, and current load evidence;\n- Q06 — settlement cutoff, prefunding, rail fallback, finality, and same-day contingencies;\n- Q07 — fraud thresholds, manual review, customer state, communications, and privacy;\n- Q08 — key/token status, break-glass access, audit integrity, and retention;\n- Q09 — regulatory determination, reporting clock, aggregate loss, and evidence custody;\n- Q10 — telemetry coverage, alerts versus holds, sampling, reconciliation, and uncertainty;\n- Q11 — candidate lineage, rollback compatibility, effect uptake, current check, repair, and recheck;\n- Q12 — blockers, falsifiers, independent readiness, accepted residual risk, and closure evidence.\n\n## Relationship rules\n\nPreserve milliseconds versus seconds, transactions per second versus per\nminute, percentages versus probabilities, availability versus payment success,\ntargets versus observations, component ratings versus shared usable capacity,\nsample coverage versus loss rate, and mechanical checks versus independent\nreadiness. A candidate, schema, writer route, queue policy, service limit, key\nset, role, rail route, settlement cutoff, or sample-plan effect can make earlier\nevidence stale.\n\nThe decision must state owners, inputs, resources, timing, dependencies,\neffects, observations, contingencies, rollback and retirement conditions, and\nevidence that would falsify important claims. Do not infer that a green format\ncheck, provenance record, mutation, or submission establishes readiness.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Action contract\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object using one currently allowed action.\n\n```text\n{\"action\":\"read_source\",\"source_id\":\"ANCHOR\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":64}\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"source_id\":\"ANCHOR\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":64},{\"source_id\":\"BRIDGE\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":64}]}\n{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"}\n{\"action\":\"replace_evidence_ledger\",\"content\":\"complete compact task-native matrix\"}\n{\"action\":\"upsert_decision_section\",\"heading\":\"Authority, scope, and recovery decision\",\"body\":\"exact section body\"}\n{\"action\":\"replace_decision\",\"content\":\"complete exact decision\"}\n{\"action\":\"run_check\"}\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}\n```\n\nOne read may contain at most 120 lines. One batch may contain one or two ranges,\nat most 160 total lines, 12,000 source bytes, and 6,500 model-visible result\ntokens. Same-source ranges may not overlap. Use exact catalog IDs and in-range\nline bounds.\n\nBoth configurations have the same ordinary action surface. The treatment may\nreceive separately charged provenance-local source reports after exact source\nbodies are externalized, but those reports are not source truth, task work,\nverification, or readiness authority. Cross-source synthesis belongs in the\nexact candidate and must cite all supporting sources.\n\nChecks bind to the exact candidate version. Any later candidate effect makes\nthe prior check stale. Submission never self-authorizes readiness.\n\n\n# Common pre-fork action notice\nNo semantic-maintenance output is present during pressure screening. Both future configurations share this ordinary action surface and exact task work.\n\n# Exact source catalog\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-source-catalog-v0\",\"sources\":[{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"af665fec52c48ca6a526467d4b189a617b121f8fa56d4e64c50305493a242a07\",\"size_bytes\":4011,\"source_id\":\"ANCHOR\",\"title\":\"Incident authority, release control, and accountable closure\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"bab58815205c2583aeb82136eb64ec56536503e70a941895d7b8f0c974bc0b3a\",\"size_bytes\":4323,\"source_id\":\"BRIDGE\",\"title\":\"Ledger replication, consistency, and recovery-point evidence\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"81dadb46183523e77f835d095ffa22b3e629934fd1829b3e24f686326899c1f9\",\"size_bytes\":3632,\"source_id\":\"CIRRUS\",\"title\":\"Idempotency keys, retry windows, and duplicate-payment controls\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"cc233015a6920ee975edcd2623c2b2681c76bf31c08014de75831cd0f3d9bf8f\",\"size_bytes\":4064,\"source_id\":\"DUSK\",\"title\":\"Queue backlog, replay order, and drain constraints\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"3991d4dc25ef2d327d356fd7f9960ee3d96c3423a25db6fdc5068a9b4b64c71e\",\"size_bytes\":3529,\"source_id\":\"EMBER\",\"title\":\"Service capacity, dependency headroom, and traffic ramps\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"83800848a2b3281e05b3e7b550b9df0872e698db65b0ab5ad5380934b132e402\",\"size_bytes\":3472,\"source_id\":\"FORGE\",\"title\":\"Settlement cutoffs, funding, and ledger finality\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"ec5a80fea342404bbfe9a0e61c819143ed45d65aa55be54a204e1467c3f1ec20\",\"size_bytes\":3782,\"source_id\":\"GROVE\",\"title\":\"Fraud controls, hold thresholds, and manual review capacity\"},{\"line_count\":64,\"sha256\":\"41b36ac861ee435e24cf545016108755ae489ba89c13e78cf6df2100e6c7092f\",\"size_bytes\":3953,\"source_id\":\"HARBOR\",\"title\":\"Cus