urchasing does not waive access review, ledger consistency, idempotency, settlement, or regulatory controls. Closure requires accountable-executive acceptance of every declared blocker and residual risk.\nA handoff is valid only when the receiving owner acknowledges the same recovery-candidate, ledger-schema, queue-policy, and key-set versions. An unacknowledged version mismatch blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nBRIDGE and CIRRUS supply ledger and retry evidence but cannot authorize restoration. PRISM supplies independent readiness findings but does not execute the release.\nNOVA owns rollback mechanics; ANCHOR retains authority separation among detection, recommendation, authorization, execution, verification, and closure.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | object/region | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUTH-000 | incident-command | v3 | 1.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUTH-001 | risk-owner | v3 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-002 | settlement-owner | v3 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-003 | regulator | v3 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-004 | incident-command | v3 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-005 | risk-owner | v3 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-006 | settlement-owner | v3 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-007 | regulator | v3 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-008 | incident-command | v3 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-009 | risk-owner | v3 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-010 | settlement-owner | v3 | 3.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-011 | regulator | v3 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-012 | incident-command | v3 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-013 | risk-owner | v3 | 3.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-014 | settlement-owner | v4 | 1.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-015 | regulator | v4 | 3.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-016 | incident-command | v4 | 1.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-017 | risk-owner | v4 | 2.3 | approval | superseded |\n| AUTH-018 